  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Another rounds of showers and thunderstorms expected today,\nwith an isolated strong storm possible.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nCluster of storms over nrn New England ahead of s/wv will likely\ncontinue moving south and east overnight and remain just outside\nof the CWA thru daybreak. Latest HRRR has the best handle on\ncurrent location and shows complex dropping into srn NH with a\npossible shower just brushing Bangor and the MDI area after 12z. \n\nAfter initial wave this morning bringing showers to southern\nareas several waves will be dropping thru the CWA this \nafternoon. Parameters for severe storms are lacking with CAPES\nranging from 500-800 J/kg and marginal lapse rates. 0-6km shear\nvalues range from 15kts over the north to 30kts Downeast. PW\nvalues only increase to about 1.25 inches. May see a few gusty\nstorms to develop throughout the afternoon but overall not a\nwidespread wetting rain expected. \n\nHigh pressure builds in for the weekend and will continue to worsen \nthe ongoing dry/drought conditions. D0-D1 conditions are present in \nsouthern and eastern areas of the CWA. Much of the streamflows \nacross the CWA are Below to Much Below Normal for this time of year \nalong with Groundwater wells rapidly falling to below normal to low \nend normal conditions. Lack of significant widespread rainfall will \nresult in worsening conditions in terms of the drought.",
